cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LAD-DA3: LiDAR-Anchored Depth for foundation depth models"
message: "If you use this work, please cite as below."
type: software
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-04-29
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: TBD
    given-names: TBD
abstract: >-
  We propose Height-Anchored Depth (HAD), a test-time procedure that
  recovers metric depth from foundation depth models in roadside / V2X
  scenes by anchoring on world-frame object heights extracted from sparse
  LiDAR returns inside instance segmentation masks, instead of the
  conventional camera-axis-depth anchors. HAD yields a closed-form
  per-instance affine fit and outperforms global / region z-anchor
  baselines especially in the long-range regime.
keywords:
  - depth-estimation
  - foundation-models
  - lidar
  - v2x
  - roadside-perception
